{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1358031-can-sin-eater-geist-make-for-a-good-horror-game","id":1358031,"title":"Can Sin-Eater: Geist make for a good horror game?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-12-31T10:27:14-08:00","id":1358031,"title":"Can Sin-Eater: Geist make for a good horror game?","content":"Since it deals with ghost and all that jazz. There has been many horror game involving ghosts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1945-magicballz","name":"Magicballz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"175"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-31T10:51:14-08:00","id":1358036,"title":"","content":"Short answer: Yes.<br /> <br /> Long answer: Hell fucking yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-01T09:03:16-08:00","id":1358204,"title":"","content":"My top tips for creating a horror atmosphere at the tabletop (Specifically for Monster stories):<br /> <br /> \u2022 Obscure the Monster. No name, very fleeting glimpses of the creature. Having a name like \u201cWerewolf\u201d, \u201cJack the Ripper\u201d, etc... adds a sense of security. It gives the sense of knowing what the monster\u2019s weakness and history is. This information should be discovered over the course of the game, not at the player\u2019s disposal from the start. <br /> <br /> \u2022 Leave a Trail of Bodies. If your players are power gamers or very attached to their characters you may want to foreshadow the power of the monster. If the creature only kills rarely make sure your players at least see what it is capable of. Don\u2019t explain how the body was killed, but what the corpse looks like and possible explanations as to what might have happened. Let the players try to use their imagination to fill in the gaps.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Keep descriptions and explanations open for interpretation. Player\u2019s minds are better at scaring themselves than your colorful descriptions will ever be.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Horror is an art form and takes practice. If something doesn\u2019t work don\u2019t back pedal. Let it stand and try to come up with why it didn\u2019t land the way you hoped. Then adjust later on and make improvements.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Escalate slowly. A half glimpsed shadow is scarier than a murderer just stabbing a person in broad daylight. Start with small horror elements like creeky floor boards and flickering lights. Then move up progressively to dripping blood from the ceiling and rotting corpses hanging from meat hooks. The goal is creepy/suspenseful; not just out right disgust.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","user":"DontEatRawHagis","date":". 01-01-2020, 12:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","name":"DontEatRawHagis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}